{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 77,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.77.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the chief Musician, to Jeduthun, A Psalm of Asaph. I cried to God with my voice, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to God with my voice; and he gave ear to me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.77.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the day of my trouble I sought the LORD: my sore ran in the night, and ceased not: my soul refused to be comforted.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.77.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I remembered God, and was troubled: I complained, and my spirit was overwhelmed. Selah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.77.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou holdest my eyes waking: I am so troubled that I cannot speak.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.77.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have considered the days of old, the years of ancient times.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.77.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I call to remembrance my song in the night: I commune with my own heart: and my spirit made diligent search.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.77.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Will the LORD cast off for ever? and will he be favorable no more?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.77.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is his mercy wholly gone for ever? doth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " promise fail for evermore?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.77.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hath God forgotten to be gracious? hath he in anger shut up his tender mercies? Selah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.77.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I said, This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my infirmity: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but I will remember",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the years of the right hand of the Most High.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.77.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will remember the works of the LORD: surely I will remember thy wonders of old.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.77.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will meditate also of all thy work, and talk of thy doings.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.77.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy way, O God, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the sanctuary: who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " great a God as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "our",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " God!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.77.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the God that doest wonders: thou hast declared thy strength among the people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.77.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast with ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thy",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " arm redeemed thy people, the sons of Jacob and Joseph. Selah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.77.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The waters saw thee, O God, the waters saw thee; they were afraid: the depths also were disturbed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.77.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The clouds poured out water: the skies sent out a sound: thy arrows also went abroad.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.77.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The voice of thy thunder ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the heaven: the lightnings lightened the world: the earth trembled and shook.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.77.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy way ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the sea, and thy path in the great waters, and thy footsteps are not known.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.77.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou leddest thy people like a flock by the hand of Moses and Aaron.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
